Divine Intervention}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Beginning at 10th level, you can call on your deity to intervene on your behalf when your need is great.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Imploring your deity\u8217\'92s aid requires you to use your action. Describe the assistance you seek, and roll percentile dice. If you roll a number equal to or lower than your cleric level, your deity intervenes.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The GM chooses the nature of the intervention; the effect of any cleric spell or cleric domain spell would be appropriate.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
If your deity intervenes, you can\u8217\'92t use this feature again for 7 days. Otherwise, you can use it again after you finish a long rest.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart section-cleric}{\*\bkmkstart cleric}{\*\bkmkend section-cleric}{\*\bkmkend cleric}
At 20th level, your call for intervention succeeds automatically, no roll required.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Domains}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Life Domain}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The Life domain focuses on the vibrant positive energy\u8212\'97one of the fundamental forces of the universe\u8212\'97that sustains all life. The }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#chapter-pantheons" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
gods of life}{}}}\loch
 promote vitality and health through healing the sick and wounded, caring for those in need, and driving away the forces of death and undeath. Almost any non-evil deity can claim influence over this domain, particularly agricultural deities (such as Isis, The Daghdha, and Demeter), sun gods (such as Belenus, Frey, and Re-Horakhty), gods of healing or endurance (such as Apollo, Lugh, and Diancecht), and gods of home and community (such as Hestia, Hathor, and Frigga).}
\par \pard\plain \s79\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa120\keepn\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f7\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
