The Druid Spell Slots per Level table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your spells of 1st level and higher. To cast one of these druid spells, you must expend a slot of the spell\u8217\'92s level or higher. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a long rest.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You prepare the list of druid spells that are available for you to cast, choosing from the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-druid-spells" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
druid spell list}{}}}\loch
. When you do so, choose a number of druid spells equal to your Wisdom modifier + your druid level (minimum of one spell). The spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
For example, if you are a 3rd-level druid, you have four 1st-level and two 2nd-level spell slots. With a Wisdom of 16, your list of prepared spells can include six spells of 1st or 2nd level, in any combination. If you prepare the 1st-level spell }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#cure-wounds" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
cure wounds}{}}}\loch
, you can cast it using a 1st-level or 2nd-level slot. Casting the spell doesn\u8217\'92t remove it from your list of prepared spells.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart preparing-and-casting-spells-1}{\*\bkmkend preparing-and-casting-spells-1}
You can also change your list of prepared spells when you finish a long rest. Preparing a new list of druid spells requires time spent in prayer and meditation: at least 1 minute per spell level for each spell on your list.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Spellcasting Ability}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for your druid spells, since your magic draws upon your devotion and attunement to nature. You use your Wisdom whenever a spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Wisdom modifier when setting the saving throw DC for a druid spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.}
\par \trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9252\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Spell save DC}{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
 = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9252\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Spell attack modifier}{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch{\*\bkmkstart spellcasting-ability-2}{\*\bkmkend spellcasting-ability-2}
 = your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier}\cell\row\pard\pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Ritual Casting}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You can cast a druid spell as a ritual if that spell has the ritual tag and you have the spell prepared.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Spellcasting Focus}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You can use a }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-adventuring-gear" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
druidic focus}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart spellcasting-2}{\*\bkmkstart spellcasting-focus-2}{\*\bkmkend spellcasting-2}{\*\bkmkend spellcasting-focus-2}
 as a spellcasting focus for your druid spells.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Wild Shape}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Starting at 2nd level, you can use your action to magically assume the shape of a beast that you have seen before. You can use this feature twice. You regain expended uses when you finish a short or long rest.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Your druid level determines the beasts you can transform into, as shown in the Beast Shapes table. At 2nd level, for example, you can transform into any beast that has a challenge rating of 1/4 or lower that doesn\u8217\'92t have a flying or swimming speed.}
\par \pard\plain \s79\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa120\keepn\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f7\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Beast Shapes}
\par \trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx921\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx2138\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5882\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx7567\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Level}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Max. CR}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Limitations}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Example}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx921\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx2138\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5882\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx7567\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
2nd}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
1/4}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
No flying or swimming speed}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Wolf}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx921\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx2138\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5882\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx7567\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
4th}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
1/2}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
No flying speed}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Crocodile}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx921\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx2138\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5882\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx7567\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
8th}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
1}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i
\u8212\'97}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Giant eagle}\cell\row\pard\pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You can stay in a beast shape for a number of hours equal to half your druid level (rounded down). You then revert to your normal form unless you expend another use of this feature. You can revert to your normal form earlier by using a bonus action on your turn. You automatically revert if you fall }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#unconscious" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
unconscious}{}}}\loch
, drop to 0 hit points, or die.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
While you are transformed, the following rules apply:}
\par \pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\listtext\pard\plain  \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls24 \li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-480{\loch
Your game statistics are replaced by the statistics of the beast, but you retain your alignment, personality, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. You also retain all of your skill and saving throw proficiencies, in addition to gaining those of the creature. If the creature has the same proficiency as you and the bonus in its stat block is higher than yours, use the creature\u8217\'92s bonus instead of yours. If the creature has any legendary or lair actions, you can\u8217\'92t use them.}
\par \pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\listtext\pard\plain  \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls24 \li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-480{\loch
When you transform, you assume the beast\u8217\'92s hit points and Hit Dice. When you revert to your normal form, you return to the number of hit points you had before you transformed. However, if you revert as a result of dropping to 0 hit points, any excess damage carries over to your normal form. For example, if you take 10 damage in animal form and have only 1 hit point left, you revert and take 9 damage. As long as the excess damage doesn\u8217\'92t reduce your normal form to 0 hit points, you aren\u8217\'92t knocked }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#unconscious" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
unconscious}{}}}\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\listtext\pard\plain  \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls24 \li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-480{\loch
You can\u8217\'92t cast spells, and your ability to speak or take any action that requires hands is limited to the capabilities of your beast form. Transforming doesn\u8217\'92t break your concentration on a spell you\u8217\'92ve already cast, however, or prevent you from taking actions that are part of a spell, such as }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#call-lightning" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
call lightning}{}}}\loch
, that you\u8217\'92ve already cast.}
\par \pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\listtext\pard\plain  \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls24 \li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-480{\loch
You retain the benefit of any features from your class, race, or other source and can use them if the new form is physically capable of doing so. However, you can\u8217\'92t use any of your special senses, such as darkvision, unless your new form also has that sense.}
\par \pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\listtext\pard\plain  \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls24 \li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-480{\loch{\*\bkmkstart wild-shape}{\*\bkmkend wild-shape}
You choose whether your equipment falls to the ground in your space, merges into your new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal, but the GM decides whether it is practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment, based on the creature\u8217\'92s shape and size. Your equipment doesn\u8217\'92t change size or shape to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can\u8217\'92t wear must either fall to the ground or merge with it. Equipment that merges with the form has no effect until you leave the form.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Druid Circle}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
At 2nd level, you choose to identify with a }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-druid-circles" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
circle of druids}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart druid-circle}{\*\bkmkend druid-circle}
. Your choice grants you features at 2nd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Timeless Body}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart timeless-body}{\*\bkmkend timeless-body}
Starting at 18th level, the primal magic that you wield causes you to age more slowly. For every 10 years that pass, your body ages only 1 year.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Ability Score Improvement}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart ability-score-improvement-3}{\*\bkmkend ability-score-improvement-3}
When you reach 4th level, and again at 8th, 12th, 16th, and 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can\u8217\'92t increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Beast Spells}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart beast-spells}{\*\bkmkend beast-spells}
Beginning at 18th level, you can cast many of your druid spells in any shape you assume using Wild Shape. You can perform the somatic and verbal components of a druid spell while in a beast shape, but you aren\u8217\'92t able to provide material components.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Archdruid}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
At 20th level, you can use your Wild Shape an unlimited number of times.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Additionally, you can ignore the verbal and somatic components of your druid spells, as well as any material components that lack a cost and aren\u8217\'92t consumed by a spell. You gain this benefit in both your normal shape and your beast shape from Wild Shape.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{{\*\bkmkstart sacred-plants-and-wood}\loch{\*\bkmkend sacred-plants-and-wood}
Sacred Plants and Wood}
\par \pard\plain \s75\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li480\ri480\lin480\rin480\fi0\sb100\sa100\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
A druid holds certain plants to be sacred, particularly alder, ash, birch, elder, hazel, holly, juniper, mistletoe, oak, rowan, willow, and yew. Druids often use such plants as part of a spellcasting focus, incorporating lengths of oak or yew or sprigs of mistletoe.}
\par \pard\plain \s75\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li480\ri480\lin480\rin480\fi0\sb100\sa100\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Similarly, a druid uses such woods to make other objects, such as weapons and shields. Yew is associated with death and rebirth, so weapon handles for scimitars or sickles might be fashioned from it. Ash is associated with life and oak with strength. These woods make excellent hafts or whole weapons, such as clubs or quarterstaffs, as well as shields. Alder is associated with air, and it might be used for thrown weapons, such as darts or javelins.}
\par \pard\plain \s75\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li480\ri480\lin480\rin480\fi0\sb100\sa100\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Druids from regions that lack the plants described here have chosen other plants to take on similar uses. For instance, a druid of a desert region might value the yucca tree and cactus plants.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{{\*\bkmkstart druids-and-the-gods}\loch{\*\bkmkend druids-and-the-gods}
Druids and the Gods}
\par \pard\plain \s75\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li480\ri480\lin480\rin480\fi0\sb100\sa100\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Some druids venerate the forces of nature themselves, but most druids are devoted to one of the many nature deities worshiped in the multiverse (the lists of gods in the \u8220\'93}{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#chapter-pantheons" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
Pantheons}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart section-druid}{\*\bkmkstart druid}{\*\bkmkstart archdruid}{\*\bkmkend section-druid}{\*\bkmkend druid}{\*\bkmkend archdruid}
\u8221\'94 section include many such deities). The worship of these deities is often considered a more ancient tradition than the faiths of clerics and urbanized peoples.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Druid Circles}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Circle of the Land}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The Circle of the Land is made up of mystics and sages who safeguard ancient knowledge and rites through a vast oral tradition. These druids meet within sacred circles of trees or standing stones to whisper primal secrets in Druidic. The circle\u8217\'92s wisest members preside as the chief priests of communities that hold to the Old Faith and serve as advisors to the rulers of those folk. As a member of this circle, your magic is influenced by the land where you were initiated into the circle\u8217\'92s mysterious rites.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Bonus Cantrip}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart bonus-cantrip}{\*\bkmkend bonus-cantrip}
When you choose this circle at 2nd level, you learn one additional druid cantrip of your choice.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Natural Recovery}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Starting at 2nd level, you can regain some of your magical energy by sitting in meditation and communing with nature. During a short rest, you choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your druid level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 6th level or higher. You can\u8217\'92t use this feature again until you finish a long rest.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart natural-recovery}{\*\bkmkend natural-recovery}
For example, when you are a 4th-level druid, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots. You can recover either a 2nd-level slot or two 1st-level slots.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Circle Spells}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Your mystical connection to the land infuses you with the ability to cast certain spells. At 3rd, 5th, 7th, and 9th level you gain access to circle spells connected to the land where you became a druid. Choose that land\u8212\'97arctic, coast, desert, forest, grassland, mountain, or swamp\u8212\'97and consult the associated list of spells.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Once you gain access to a circle spell, you always have it prepared, and it doesn\u8217\'92t count against the number of spells you can prepare each day. If you gain access to a spell that doesn\u8217\'92t appear on the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-druid-spells" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
druid spell list}{}}}\loch
, the spell is nonetheless a druid spell for you.}
\par \pard\plain \s79\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa120\keepn\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f7\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
