2}\cell\row\pard\pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The Ranger Spell Slots by Level table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your spells of 1st level and higher. To cast one of these spells, you must expend a slot of the spell\u8217\'92s level or higher. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a long rest.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
For example, if you know the 1st-level spell }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#speak-with-animals" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
speak with animals}{}}}\loch
 and have a 1st-level and a 2nd-level spell slot available, you can cast }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#speak-with-animals" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
speak with animals}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart spell-slots-1}{\*\bkmkend spell-slots-1}
 using either slot.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Spells Known of 1st Level and Higher}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You know two 1st-level spells of your choice from the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-ranger-spells" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
ranger spell list}{}}}\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The Spells Known column of the Ranger table shows when you learn more ranger spells of your choice. Each of these spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For instance, when you reach 5th level in this class, you can learn one new spell of 1st or 2nd level.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart spells-known-of-1st-level-and-higher-1}{\*\bkmkend spells-known-of-1st-level-and-higher-1}
Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the ranger spells you know and replace it with another spell from the ranger spell list, which also must be of a level for which you have spell slots.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Spellcasting Ability}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for your ranger spells, since your magic draws on your attunement to nature. You use your Wisdom whenever a spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Wisdom modifier when setting the saving throw DC for a ranger spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.}
\par \trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9252\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Spell save DC}{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
 = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9252\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Spell attack modifier}{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch{\*\bkmkstart spellcasting-4}{\*\bkmkstart spellcasting-ability-4}{\*\bkmkend spellcasting-4}{\*\bkmkend spellcasting-ability-4}
 = your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier}\cell\row\pard\pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Ranger Archetype}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
At 3rd level, you choose an }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-ranger-archetypes" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
archetype}{}}}\loch
 that you strive to emulate. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 11th, and 15th level.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Primeval Awareness}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart primeval-awareness}{\*\bkmkend primeval-awareness}
Beginning at 3rd level, you can use your action and expend one ranger spell slot to focus your awareness on the region around you. For 1 minute per level of the spell slot you expend, you can sense whether the following types of creatures are present within 1 mile of you (or within up to 6 miles if you are in your favored terrain): aberrations, celestials, dragons, elementals, fey, fiends, and undead. This feature doesn\u8217\'92t reveal the creatures\u8217\'92 location or number.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Ability Score Improvement}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart ability-score-improvement-7}{\*\bkmkend ability-score-improvement-7}
When you reach 4th level, and again at 8th, 12th, 16th, and 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can\u8217\'92t increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Extra Attack}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart extra-attack-4}{\*\bkmkend extra-attack-4}
Beginning at 5th level, you can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Land\u8217\'92s Stride}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Starting at 8th level, moving through nonmagical difficult terrain costs you no extra movement. You can also pass through nonmagical plants without being slowed by them and without taking damage from them if they have thorns, spines, or a similar hazard.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
In addition, you have advantage on saving throws against plants that are magically created or manipulated to impede movement, such those created by the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#entangle" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
entangle}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart lands-stride-1}{\*\bkmkend lands-stride-1}
 spell.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Hide in Plain Sight}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Starting at 10th level, you can spend 1 minute creating camouflage for yourself. You must have access to fresh mud, dirt, plants, soot, and other naturally occurring materials with which to create your camouflage.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart hide-in-plain-sight}{\*\bkmkend hide-in-plain-sight}
Once you are camouflaged in this way, you can try to hide by pressing yourself up against a solid surface, such as a tree or wall, that is at least as tall and wide as you are. You gain a +10 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) checks as long as you remain there without moving or taking actions. Once you move or take an action or a reaction, you must camouflage yourself again to gain this benefit.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Vanish}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart vanish}{\*\bkmkend vanish}
Starting at 14th level, you can use the Hide action as a bonus action on your turn. Also, you can\u8217\'92t be tracked by nonmagical means, unless you choose to leave a trail.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Feral Senses}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
At 18th level, you gain preternatural senses that help you fight creatures you can\u8217\'92t see. When you attack a creature you can\u8217\'92t see, your inability to see it doesn\u8217\'92t impose disadvantage on your attack rolls against it. You are also aware of the location of any }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#invisible" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
invisible}{}}}\loch
 creature within 30 feet of you, provided that the creature isn\u8217\'92t hidden from you and you aren\u8217\'92t }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#blinded" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
blinded}{}}}\loch
 or }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#deafened" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
deafened}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart feral-senses}{\*\bkmkend feral-senses}
.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Foe Slayer}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart section-ranger}{\*\bkmkstart ranger}{\*\bkmkstart foe-slayer}{\*\bkmkend section-ranger}{\*\bkmkend ranger}{\*\bkmkend foe-slayer}
At 20th level, you become an unparalleled hunter of your enemies. Once on each of your turns, you can add your Wisdom modifier to the attack roll or the damage roll of an attack you make against one of your favored enemies. You can choose to use this feature before or after the roll, but before any effects of the roll are applied.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Ranger Archetypes}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
A classic expression of the ranger ideal is the Hunter.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Hunter}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Emulating the Hunter archetype means accepting your place as a bulwark between civilization and the terrors of the wilderness. As you walk the Hunter\u8217\'92s path, you learn specialized techniques for fighting the threats you face, from rampaging ogres and hordes of orcs to towering giants and terrifying dragons.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Hunter\u8217\'92s Prey}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
At 3rd level, you gain one of the following features of your choice.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Colossus Slayer.}{\loch
 Your tenacity can wear down the most potent foes. When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, the creature takes an extra 1d8 damage if it\u8217\'92s below its hit point maximum. You can deal this extra damage only once per turn.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Giant Killer.}{\loch
 When a Large or larger creature within 5 feet of you hits or misses you with an attack, you can use your reaction to attack that creature immediately after its attack, provided that you can see the creature.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Horde Breaker.}{\loch{\*\bkmkstart hunters-prey}{\*\bkmkend hunters-prey}
 Once on each of your turns when you make a weapon attack, you can make another attack with the same weapon against a different creature that is within 5 feet of the original target and within range of your weapon.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Defensive Tactics}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
At 7th level, you gain one of the following features of your choice.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Escape the Horde.}{\loch
 Opportunity attacks against you are made with disadvantage.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Multiattack Defense.}{\loch
 When a creature hits you with an attack, you gain a +4 bonus to AC against all subsequent attacks made by that creature for the rest of the turn.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Steel Will.}{\loch
 You have advantage on saving throws against being }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#frightened" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
frightened}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart defensive-tactics}{\*\bkmkend defensive-tactics}
.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
