Once I pick a goal, I become obsessed with it to the detriment of everything else in my life.}\cell\row\pard\pard\plain \s1\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs32\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb480\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs48\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Feats}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
A feat represents a talent or an area of expertise that gives a character special capabilities. It embodies training, experience, and abilities beyond what a class provides.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
At certain levels, your class gives you the Ability Score Improvement feature. Using the optional feats rule, you can forgo taking that feature to take a feat of your choice instead. You can take each feat only once, unless the feat\u8217\'92s description says otherwise.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You must meet any prerequisite specified in a feat to take that feat. If you ever lose a feat\u8217\'92s prerequisite, you can\u8217\'92t use that feat until you regain the prerequisite. For example, the Grappler feat requires you to have a Strength of 13 or higher. If your Strength is reduced below 13 somehow\u8212\'97perhaps by a withering curse\u8212\'97you can\u8217\'92t benefit from the Grappler feat until your Strength is restored.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Grappler}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
Prerequisite: Strength 13 or higher}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You\u8217\'92ve developed the skills necessary to hold your own in close-quarters grappling. You gain the following benefits:}
\par \pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\listtext\pard\plain  \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls49 \li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-480{\loch
You have advantage on attack rolls against a creature you are grappling.}
\par \pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\listtext\pard\plain  \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls49 \li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-480{\loch
You can use your action to try to pin a creature }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#grappled" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
grappled}{}}}\loch
 by you. To do so, make another grapple check. If you succeed, you and the creature are both }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#restrained" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
restrained}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart section-grappler}{\*\bkmkstart grappler}{\*\bkmkend section-grappler}{\*\bkmkend grappler}
 until the grapple ends.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Inspiration}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Inspiration is a rule the game master can use to reward you for playing your character in a way that\u8217\'92s true to his or her personality traits, ideal, bond, and flaw. By using inspiration, you can draw on your personality trait of compassion for the downtrodden to give you an edge in negotiating with the Beggar Prince. Or inspiration can let you call on your bond to the defense of your home village to push past the effect of a spell that has been laid on you.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Gaining Inspiration}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Your GM can choose to give you inspiration for a variety of reasons. Typically, GMs award it when you play out your personality traits, give in to the drawbacks presented by a flaw or bond, and otherwise portray your character in a compelling way. Your GM will tell you how you can earn inspiration in the game.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart gaining-inspiration}{\*\bkmkend gaining-inspiration}
You either have inspiration or you don\u8217\'92t\u8212\'97you can\u8217\'92t stockpile multiple \u8220\'93inspirations\u8221\'94 for later use.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Using Inspiration}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
If you have inspiration, you can expend it when you make an attack roll, saving throw, or ability check. Spending your inspiration gives you advantage on that roll.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart section-inspiration}{\*\bkmkstart inspiration}{\*\bkmkstart using-inspiration}{\*\bkmkend section-inspiration}{\*\bkmkend inspiration}{\*\bkmkend using-inspiration}
Additionally, if you have inspiration, you can reward another player for good roleplaying, clever thinking, or simply doing something exciting in the game. When another player character does something that really contributes to the story in a fun and interesting way, you can give up your inspiration to give that character inspiration.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs32\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb480\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs48\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
The Planes of Existence}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The cosmos teems with a multitude of worlds as well as myriad alternate dimensions of reality, called the }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
planes of existence.}{\loch
 It encompasses every world where GMs run their adventures, all within the relatively mundane realm of the material plane. Beyond that plane are domains of raw elemental matter and energy, realms of pure thought and ethos, the homes of demons and angels, and the dominions of the gods.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Many spells and magic items can draw energy from these planes, summon the creatures that dwell there, communicate with their denizens, and allow adventurers to travel there. As your character achieves greater power and higher levels, you might walk on streets made of solid fire or test your mettle on a battlefield where the fallen are resurrected with each dawn.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
The Material Plane}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The material plane is the nexus where the philosophical and elemental forces that define the other planes collide in the jumbled existence of mortal life and mundane matter. All fantasy gaming worlds exist within the material plane, making it the starting point for most campaigns and adventures. The rest of the multiverse is defined in relation to the material plane.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart section-the-material-plane}{\*\bkmkstart the-material-plane}{\*\bkmkend section-the-material-plane}{\*\bkmkend the-material-plane}
The worlds of the material plane are infinitely diverse, for they reflect the creative imagination of the GMs who set their games there, as well as the players whose heroes adventure there. They include magic-wasted desert planets and island-dotted water worlds, worlds where magic combines with advanced technology and others trapped in an endless Stone Age, worlds where the gods walk and places they have abandoned.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Beyond the Material}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Beyond the material plane, the various planes of existence are realms of myth and mystery. They\u8217\'92re not simply other worlds, but different qualities of being, formed and governed by spiritual and elemental principles abstracted from the ordinary world.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Planar Travel}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
When adventurers travel into other planes of existence, they are undertaking a legendary journey across the thresholds of existence to a mythic destination where they strive to complete their quest. Such a journey is the stuff of legend. Braving the realms of the dead, seeking out the celestial servants of a deity, or bargaining with an efreeti in its home city will be the subject of song and story for years to come.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Travel to the planes beyond the material plane can be accomplished in two ways: by casting a spell or by using a planar portal.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Spells.}{\loch
 A number of spells allow direct or indirect access to other planes of existence. }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#plane-shift" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
Plane shift}{}}}\loch
 and }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#gate" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
gate}{}}}\loch
 can transport adventurers directly to any other plane of existence, with different degrees of precision. }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#etherealness" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
Etherealness}{}}}\loch
 allows adventurers to enter the ethereal plane and travel from there to any of the planes it touches\u8212\'97such as the elemental planes. And the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#astral-projection" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
astral projection}{}}}\loch
 spell lets adventurers project themselves into the astral plane and travel to the outer planes.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Portals.}{\loch{\*\bkmkstart planar-travel}{\*\bkmkend planar-travel}
 A portal is a general term for a stationary interplanar connection that links a specific location on one plane to a specific location on another. Some portals are like doorways, a clear window, or a fog-shrouded passage, and simply stepping through it effects the interplanar travel. Others are locations\u8212\'97circles of standing stones, soaring towers, sailing ships, or even whole towns\u8212\'97that exist in multiple planes at once or flicker from one plane to another in turn. Some are vortices, typically joining an elemental plane with a very similar location on the material plane, such as the heart of a volcano (leading to the fire plane) or the depths of the ocean (to the water plane).}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Transitive Planes}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The ethereal plane and the astral plane are called the }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
transitive planes}{\loch
. They are mostly featureless realms that serve primarily as ways to travel from one plane to another. Spells such as }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#etherealness" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
etherealness}{}}}\loch
 and }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#astral-projection" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
astral projection}{}}}\loch
 allow characters to enter these planes and traverse them to reach the planes beyond.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
ethereal plane}{\loch
 is a misty, fog-bound dimension that is sometimes described as a great ocean. Its shores, called the ethereal border, overlap the material plane and the inner planes, so that every location on those planes has a corresponding location on the ethereal plane. Certain creatures can see into the ethereal border, and the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#see-invisibility" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
see invisibility}{}}}\loch
 and }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#true-seeing" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
true seeing}{}}}\loch
 spell grant that ability. Some magical effects also extend from the material plane into the ethereal border, particularly effects that use force energy such as }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#forcecage" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
forcecage}{}}}\loch
 and }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#wall-of-force" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
wall of force}{}}}\loch
. The depths of the plane, the Deep Ethereal, are a region of swirling mists and colorful fogs.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
astral plane}{\loch{\*\bkmkstart transitive-planes}{\*\bkmkend transitive-planes}
 is the realm of thought and dream, where visitors travel as disembodied souls to reach the planes of the divine and demonic. It is a great, silvery sea, the same above and below, with swirling wisps of white and gray streaking among motes of light resembling distant stars. Erratic whirlpools of color flicker in midair like spinning coins. Occasional bits of solid matter can be found here, but most of the astral plane is an endless, open domain.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Inner Planes}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The inner planes surround and enfold the material plane and its echoes, providing the raw elemental substance from which all the worlds were made. The four }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
elemental planes}{\loch
\u8212\'97air, earth, fire, and water\u8212\'97form a ring around the material plane, suspended within the churning }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
primordial chaos}{\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart inner-planes}{\*\bkmkend inner-planes}
At their innermost edges, where they are closest to the material plane (in a conceptual if not a literal geographical sense), the four elemental planes resemble a world in the material plane. The four elements mingle together as they do in the material plane, forming land, sea, and sky. Farther from the material plane, though, the elemental planes are both alien and hostile. Here, the elements exist in their purest form\u8212\'97great expanses of solid earth, blazing fire, crystal\u8212\'97clear water, and unsullied air. These regions are little-known, so when discussing the fire plane, for example, a speaker usually means just the border region. At the farthest extents of the inner planes, the pure elements dissolve and bleed together into an unending tumult of clashing energies and colliding substance, the primordial chaos.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Outer Planes}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
If the inner planes are the raw matter and energy that makes up the multiverse, the outer planes are the direction, thought and purpose for such construction. Accordingly, many sages refer to the outer planes as divine planes, spiritual planes, or godly planes, for the outer planes are best known as the homes of deities.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
When discussing anything to do with deities, the language used must be highly metaphorical. Their actual homes are not literally \u8220\'93places\u8221\'94 at all, but exemplify the idea that the outer planes are realms of thought and spirit. As with the elemental planes, one can imagine the perceptible part of the outer planes as a sort of border region, while extensive spiritual regions lie beyond ordinary sensory experience.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Even in those perceptible regions, appearances can be deceptive. Initially, many of the outer planes appear hospitable and familiar to natives of the material plane. But the landscape can change at the whims of the powerful forces that live on the outer planes. The desires of the mighty forces that dwell on these planes can remake them completely, effectively erasing and rebuilding existence itself to better fulfill their own needs.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Distance is a virtually meaningless concept on the outer planes. The perceptible regions of the planes often seem quite small, but they can also stretch on to what seems like infinity. It might be possible to take a guided tour of Hell in a single day\u8212\'97if the powers of Hell desire it. Or it could take weeks for travelers to make a grueling trek across a single region.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The most well-known outer planes are a group of sixteen planes that correspond to the eight alignments (excluding neutrality) and the shades of distinction between them.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Planar Alignment}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The planes with some element of good in their nature are called the }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
upper planes.}{\loch
 Celestial creatures such as angels and pegasi dwell in the upper planes. Planes with some element of evil are the }{\rtlch\ab \ltrch\b\loch
lower planes.}{\loch{\*\bkmkstart planar-alignment}{\*\bkmkend planar-alignment}
 Fiends such as demons and devils dwell in the lower planes. A plane\u8217\'92s alignment is its essence, and a character whose alignment doesn\u8217\'92t match the plane\u8217\'92s experiences a profound sense of dissonance there. When a good creature visits a neutral good-aligned upper plane, for example, it feels in tune with the plane, but an evil creature feels out of tune and more than a little uncomfortable.}
\par \pard\plain \s4\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Demiplanes}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Demiplanes are small extradimensional spaces with their own unique rules. They are pieces of reality that don\u8217\'92t seem to fit anywhere else. Demiplanes come into being by a variety of means. Some are created by spells, such as }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#demiplane" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
demiplane}{}}}\loch
, or generated at the desire of a powerful deity or other force. They may exist naturally, as a fold of existing reality that has been pinched off from the rest of the multiverse, or as a baby universe growing in power. A given demiplane can be entered through a single point where it touches another plane. Theoretically, a }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#plane-shift" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
plane shift}{}}}\loch
 spell can also carry travelers to a demiplane, but the proper frequency required for the tuning fork is extremely hard to acquire. The }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#gate" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
gate}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart chapter-the-planes-of-existence}{\*\bkmkstart the-planes-of-existence}{\*\bkmkstart section-beyond-the-material}{\*\bkmkstart beyond-the-material}{\*\bkmkstart outer-planes}{\*\bkmkstart demiplanes}{\*\bkmkend chapter-the-planes-of-existence}{\*\bkmkend the-planes-of-existence}{\*\bkmkend section-beyond-the-material}{\*\bkmkend beyond-the-material}{\*\bkmkend outer-planes}{\*\bkmkend demiplanes}
 spell is more reliable, assuming the caster knows of the demiplane.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs32\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb480\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs48\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Pantheons}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The Celtic, Egyptian, Greek, and Norse pantheons are fantasy interpretations of historical religions from our world\u8217\'92s ancient times. They include deities that are most appropriate for use in a game, divorced from their historical context in the real world and united into pantheons that serve the needs of the game.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs28\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs36\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
The Celtic Pantheon}
\par \pard\plain \s79\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa120\keepn\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f7\fs24\lang1033\i0\b\kerning0{\loch
Celtic Deities}
\par \trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx4010\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5226\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx6443\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9064\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Deity}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Alignment}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Suggested Domains}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Symbol}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx4010\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5226\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx6443\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9064\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
The Daghdha, god of weather and crops}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
CG}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Nature, Trickery}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Bubbling cauldron or shield}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx4010\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5226\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx6443\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9064\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Arawn, god of life and death}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\qc\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
NE}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Life, Death}\cell\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
Black star on gray background}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\trleft-108\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx4010\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5226\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx6443\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx9064\pard\plain \s68\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb36\sa36\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\intbl\ql\nowidctlpar\sb36\sa36{\rtlch \ltrch\i\loch
