* Found only in a deck with twenty-two cards}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Balance.}{\loch
 Your mind suffers a wrenching alteration, causing your alignment to change. Lawful becomes chaotic, good becomes evil, and vice versa. If you are true neutral or unaligned, this card has no effect on you.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Comet.}{\loch
 If you single-handedly defeat the next hostile monster or group of monsters you encounter, you gain experience points enough to gain one level. Otherwise, this card has no effect.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Donjon.}{\loch
 You disappear and become entombed in a state of suspended animation in an extradimensional sphere. Everything you were wearing and carrying stays behind in the space you occupied when you disappeared. You remain imprisoned until you are found and removed from the sphere. You can\u8217\'92t be located by any divination magic, but a }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#wish" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
wish}{}}}\loch
 spell can reveal the location of your prison. You draw no more cards.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Euryale.}{\loch
 The card\u8217\'92s medusa-like visage curses you. You take a -2 penalty on saving throws while cursed in this way. Only a god or the magic of The Fates card can end this curse.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
The Fates.}{\loch
 Reality\u8217\'92s fabric unravels and spins anew, allowing you to avoid or erase one event as if it never happened. You can use the card\u8217\'92s magic as soon as you draw the card or at any other time before you die.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Flames.}{\loch
 A powerful devil becomes your enemy. The devil seeks your ruin and plagues your life, savoring your suffering before attempting to slay you. This enmity lasts until either you or the devil dies.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Fool.}{\loch
 You lose 10,000 XP, discard this card, and draw from the deck again, counting both draws as one of your declared draws. If losing that much XP would cause you to lose a level, you instead lose an amount that leaves you with just enough XP to keep your level.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Gem.}{\loch
 Twenty-five pieces of jewelry worth 2,000 gp each or fifty gems worth 1,000 gp each appear at your feet.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Idiot.}{\loch
 Permanently reduce your Intelligence by 1d4 + 1 (to a minimum score of 1). You can draw one additional card beyond your declared draws.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Jester.}{\loch
 You gain 10,000 XP, or you can draw two additional cards beyond your declared draws.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Key.}{\loch
 A rare or rarer magic weapon with which you are proficient appears in your hands. The GM chooses the weapon.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Knight.}{\loch
 You gain the service of a 4th-level fighter who appears in a space you choose within 30 feet of you. The fighter is of the same race as you and serves you loyally until death, believing the fates have drawn him or her to you. You control this character.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Moon.}{\loch
 You are granted the ability to cast the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#wish" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
wish}{}}}\loch
 spell 1d3 times.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Rogue.}{\loch
 A nonplayer character of the GM\u8217\'92s choice becomes hostile toward you. The identity of your new enemy isn\u8217\'92t known until the NPC or someone else reveals it. Nothing less than a }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#wish" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
wish}{}}}\loch
 spell or divine intervention can end the NPC\u8217\'92s hostility toward you.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Ruin.}{\loch
 All forms of wealth that you carry or own, other than magic items, are lost to you. Portable property vanishes. Businesses, buildings, and land you own are lost in a way that alters reality the least. Any documentation that proves you should own something lost to this card also disappears.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Skull.}{\loch
 You summon an }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#avatar-of-death" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
avatar of death}{}}}\loch
\u8212\'97a ghostly humanoid skeleton clad in a tattered black robe and carrying a spectral scythe. It appears in a space of the GM\u8217\'92s choice within 10 feet of you and attacks you, warning all others that you must win the battle alone. The avatar fights until you die or it drops to 0 hit points, whereupon it disappears. If anyone tries to help you, the helper summons its own avatar of death. A creature slain by an avatar of death can\u8217\'92t be restored to life.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Star.}{\loch
 Increase one of your ability scores by 2. The score can exceed 20 but can\u8217\'92t exceed 24.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Sun.}{\loch
 You gain 50,000 XP, and a wondrous item (which the GM determines randomly) appears in your hands.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Talons.}{\loch
 Every magic item you wear or carry disintegrates. Artifacts in your possession aren\u8217\'92t destroyed but do vanish.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Throne.}{\loch
 You gain proficiency in the Persuasion skill, and you double your proficiency bonus on checks made with that skill. In addition, you gain rightful ownership of a small keep somewhere in the world. However, the keep is currently in the hands of monsters, which you must clear out before you can claim the keep as yours.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Vizier.}{\loch
 At any time you choose within one year of drawing this card, you can ask a question in meditation and mentally receive a truthful answer to that question. Besides information, the answer helps you solve a puzzling problem or other dilemma. In other words, the knowledge comes with wisdom on how to apply it.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
The Void.}{\loch
 This black card spells disaster. Your soul is drawn from your body and contained in an object in a place of the GM\u8217\'92s choice. One or more powerful beings guard the place. While your soul is trapped in this way, your body is }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#incapacitated" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
incapacitated}{}}}\loch
. A }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#wish" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
wish}{}}}\loch
 spell can\u8217\'92t restore your soul, but the spell reveals the location of the object that holds it. You draw no more cards.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Defender}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
Weapon (any sword), legendary (requires }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-attunement" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
attunement}{}}}\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
)}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You gain a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart defender}{\*\bkmkend defender}
The first time you attack with the sword on each of your turns, you can transfer some or all of the sword\u8217\'92s bonus to your Armor Class, instead of using the bonus on any attacks that turn. For example, you could reduce the bonus to your attack and damage rolls to +1 and gain a +2 bonus to AC. The adjusted bonuses remain in effect until the start of your next turn, although you must hold the sword to gain a bonus to AC from it.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Demon Armor}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
Armor (plate), very rare (requires }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-attunement" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
attunement}{}}}\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
)}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, and you can understand and speak Abyssal. In addition, the armor\u8217\'92s clawed gauntlets turn unarmed strikes with your hands into magic weapons that deal slashing damage, with a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls and a damage die of 1d8.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Curse.}{\loch
 Once you don this cursed armor, you can\u8217\'92t doff it unless you are targeted by the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#remove-curse" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
remove curse}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart demon-armor}{\*\bkmkend demon-armor}
 spell or similar magic. While wearing the armor, you have disadvantage on attack rolls against demons and on saving throws against their spells and special abilities.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Dimensional Shackles}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
Wondrous item, rare}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
You can use an action to place these shackles on an }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#incapacitated" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
incapacitated}{}}}\loch
 creature. The shackles adjust to fit a creature of Small to Large size. In addition to serving as mundane manacles, the shackles prevent a creature bound by them from using any method of extradimensional movement, including teleportation or travel to a different plane of existence. They don\u8217\'92t prevent the creature from passing through an interdimensional portal.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch{\*\bkmkstart dimensional-shackles}{\*\bkmkend dimensional-shackles}
You and any creature you designate when you use the shackles can use an action to remove them. Once every 30 days, the bound creature can make a DC 30 Strength (Athletics) check. On a success, the creature breaks free and destroys the shackles.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
Dragon Scale Mail}
\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
Armor (scale mail), very rare (requires }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#section-attunement" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
attunement}{}}}\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
)}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Dragon scale mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them to humanoids. Other times, hunters carefully skin and preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, dragon scale mail is highly valued.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, you have advantage on saving throws against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of dragons, and you have resistance to one damage type that is determined by the kind of dragon that provided the scales (see the table).}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Additionally, you can focus your senses as an action to magically discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of you that is of the same type as the armor. This special action can\u8217\'92t be used again until the next dawn.}
