\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
Found in a small container, this powder resembles very fine sand. It appears to be dust of disappearance, and an }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#identify" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
identify}{}}}\loch
 spell reveals it to be such. There is enough of it for one use.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
When you use an action to throw a handful of the dust into the air, you and each creature that needs to breathe within 30 feet of you must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or become unable to breathe, while sneezing uncontrollably. A creature affected in this way is }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#incapacitated" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
incapacitated}{}}}\loch
 and suffocating.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
As long as it is conscious, a creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on it on a success. The }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#lesser-restoration" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\ai \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\i\loch
lesser restoration}{}}}\loch{\*\bkmkstart dust-of-sneezing-and-choking}{\*\bkmkend dust-of-sneezing-and-choking}
 spell can also end the effect on a creature.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af9\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ab\ql\keep\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb200\sa0\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brdrcf31\brsp20\keepn\ltrpar\cf17\loch\f4\fs32\lang1033\b\kerning0{\loch
