\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
A }{\rtlch\ai \ltrch\i\loch
spell scroll}{\loch
 bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your class\u8217\'92s }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#chapter-spell-lists" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
spell list}{}}}\loch
, you can read the scroll and cast its spell without providing any material components. Otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell by reading the scroll requires the spell\u8217\'92s normal casting time. Once the spell is cast, the words on the scroll fade, and it crumbles to dust. If the casting is uninterrupted, the scroll is not lost.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
If the spell is on your class\u8217\'92s spell list but of a higher level than you can normally cast, you must make an ability check using your spellcasting ability to determine whether you cast it successfully. The DC equals 10 + the spell\u8217\'92s level. On a failed check, the spell disappears from the scroll with no other effect.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
The level of the spell on the scroll determines the spell\u8217\'92s saving throw DC and attack bonus, as well as the scroll\u8217\'92s rarity, as shown in the Spell Scroll table.}
