\par \pard\plain \s67\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\loch
There are many easy ways to customize the NPCs in this section for your home campaign.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Racial Traits.}{\loch
 You can add racial traits to an NPC. For example, a halfling druid might have a speed of 25 feet and the Lucky trait. Adding racial traits to an NPC doesn\u8217\'92t alter its challenge rating. For more on racial traits, see \u8220\'93}{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "#chapter-races" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ltrch\hich\af4\cf17\loch\f4\fs22\loch
Races}{}}}\loch
\u8221\'94.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Spell Swaps.}{\loch
 One way to customize an NPC spellcaster is to replace one or more of its spells. You can substitute any spell on the NPC\u8217\'92s spell list with a different spell of the same level from the same spell list. Swapping spells in this manner doesn\u8217\'92t alter an NPC\u8217\'92s challenge rating.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Armor and Weapon Swaps.}{\loch
 You can upgrade or downgrade an NPC\u8217\'92s armor, or add or switch weapons. Adjustments to Armor Class and damage can change an NPC\u8217\'92s challenge rating.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\dbch\af10\langfe1033\dbch\af9\afs24\alang1025\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb180\sa180\ltrpar\cf0\loch\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0{\rtlch\ai\ab \ltrch\i\b\loch
Magic Items.}{\loch{\*\bkmkstart section-customizing-npcs}{\*\bkmkstart customizing-npcs}{\*\bkmkend section-customizing-npcs}{\*\bkmkend customizing-npcs}
 The more powerful an NPC, the more likely it has one or more magic items in its possession. An archmage, for example, might have a magic staff or wand, as well as one or more potions and scrolls. Giving an NPC a potent damage-dealing magic item could alter its challenge rating.}
